      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:47:14",
      "text": [
        " الصَّبْرُ صَبْرَانِ صَبْرٌ عَلَى الْبَلَاءِ حَسَنٌ جَمِيلٌ وَ أَفْضَلُ الصَّبْرَيْنِ الْوَرَعُ عَنِ الْمَحَارِمِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from his father, from Yunus Bin Abdul Rahman, raising it, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The patience is two (types of) patience – Patience upon the affliction is good, beautiful; and (even) superior of the two (types of) patience is the abstinence from the Prohibitions’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "14. It is narrated from him (narrator of the Hadith above) from his father from Yunus ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman who has narrated it in a marfu’ manner from abu Ja’far (a.s.) who has said the following: “Abu Ja’far (a.s.) has said, ‘Patience is of two kinds: to exercise patience in hardship, which is good and graceful, yet, the best of patience is that which is exercised to stop one from committing what Allah has prohibited.”’ "
        ]
      }
